! =============================================================================
! Tutorial Problem #7 (manual): Post-processing of Heating Steel
! =============================================================================
! System: Fe-0.15wt%C steel. Swept 500-1700 C in 50 C steps, 1 atm.
! Teaching point: produce a plot of phase fractions against temperature by
! post-processing a temperature sweep's JSON output in an external tool.
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/manual/tut07_FeC_heating_sweep.ti
! Verified phase transitions (matching the manual's Figure 4):
!   BCC_A2 (+ C_GRAPHITE) stable below ~700 C
!   BCC_A2 -> FCC_A1 transition between 700 C and 850 C (manual: 738 C)
!   FCC_A1 single phase from ~900 C to 1450 C
!   FCC_A1 -> Liquid transition between 1450 C and 1550 C (manual: ~1493 C)
! See inputs/training/manual/plot_tut07.py to render this as a chart.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 500:1700:50
pressure          = 1.0
mass(26)          = 1.787985
mass(6)           = 0.012489
temperature unit  = C
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/CuFeC-Kang.dat
print mode        = 1
write json        = .TRUE.
output            = tut07_FeC_heating
reinit            = .TRUE.
